Falsifies `system_tests::user::running_space_tests::unmap_through_a_copy_made_before_configure_faults_the_running_thread`.

Architecture: aarch64, riscv64, x86_64

The defect: a capability stops resolving once its space is bound to a thread, which is what
`CONFIGURE` retiring the name did before §249 (a running address space stays nameable). The kept
copy then reaches nothing, and `UNMAP` cannot touch the window it exists to close.

Expected to fail: the first assertion after the reader starts, which gets `Err(BadPointer)` from
`UNMAP` instead of `Ok(0)`.

diff --git a/kernel/src/user.rs b/kernel/src/user.rs
--- a/kernel/src/user.rs
+++ b/kernel/src/user.rs
@@ -703,7 +703,10 @@
